x = 3 x = 3 is the only candidate left. If you plug back in: 3 + 7 = 10 , 3 − 1 = 2 \sqrt{3+7} = \sqrt{10}, \qquad 3 - 1 = 2 3 + 7 ​ = 10 ​ , 3 − 1 = 2 Oops - this is actually worth catching: that does not match. Let's check carefully: 3 + 7 = 10 ≠ 2 \sqrt{3+7} = \sqrt{10} 
